const faqs = [
  { q: "How much can I borrow against an Audemars Piguet in Australia?", a: "ALYRA's published luxury-watch loan range is $50,000 to $5 million, and Audemars Piguet is one of the brands it considers. The amount for your watch is not set by brand alone; it depends on the individual watch, valuation, suitability as security and approval." },
  { q: "Can I borrow $50,000 against any Audemars Piguet?", a: "No. The $50,000 figure is the lower end of ALYRA's published luxury-watch loan range, not a guaranteed amount for every AP. ALYRA states that the amount available depends on the watch and its suitability as loan security." },
  { q: "What percentage of my Audemars Piguet value can I borrow?", a: "As at 14 August 2026, ALYRA's public luxury-watch page does not state a fixed Audemars Piguet loan-to-value percentage. A specialist reviews the exact watch, including its reference, condition, documents, authenticity, ownership records and current demand, before any offer is made." },
  { q: "Is a Royal Oak better security than another Audemars Piguet?", a: "There is no collection-wide rule: ALYRA states that every watch is reviewed individually. Royal Oak references span many configurations and completed 2026 auction results vary materially, so the exact reference and current market evidence matter." },
  { q: "Can I borrow against a Royal Oak Offshore?", a: "Potentially. The Royal Oak Offshore was introduced in 1993, but any loan still depends on the individual reference, condition, documents, authenticity, market demand, valuation and approval." },
  { q: "Can I borrow against a Code 11.59?", a: "Potentially. Code 11.59 by Audemars Piguet was revealed in 2019 and includes watches in different sizes, materials and complications. As with any AP, the lender needs to assess the exact watch rather than the collection name alone." },
  { q: "Do I need the box and papers for an Audemars Piguet loan?", a: "Not always. ALYRA states that box and papers can help establish authenticity and value and can support stronger terms, but they are not always essential. If they are missing, it can still be worth submitting the watch for assessment." },
  { q: "Does service history affect the loan amount?", a: "Service history is one of the factors ALYRA lists in its specialist assessment, but it does not determine the loan by itself. The lender considers it together with the reference, condition, originality, documents, rarity, demand, ownership and authenticity." },
  { q: "Do I keep ownership of my Audemars Piguet during the loan?", a: "Yes. ALYRA states that you remain the owner while the watch is held as security. If the loan is repaid under the agreed terms, the watch is returned to you." },
  { q: "What happens if I cannot repay the loan?", a: "Your watch is at risk if you do not meet the repayment obligations. ALYRA states that the relevant fees, notices, redemption rights and enforcement processes are disclosed in the written loan terms before you proceed." },
];

